    <!-- GitHub API Explanation Dialog -->
    <string name="github_explanation_title">Transparency &amp; GitHub API Limits</string>
    <string name="github_explanation_body">ShizuCoreFetch relies on GitHub servers to fetch data. Without logging in, GitHub limits your device to 60 requests per hour. Logging in grants you a quota of 5,000 requests per hour.\n\nWhy does the app need authorization?\nWe use a classic (OAuth App) which requires public repository access (public_repo) to be able to post comments (as Issues), interact with them, and fetch Shizuku app indexes from public repositories. We do not collect your data in any way, and logging in is a standard and necessary procedure to fetch and drop data efficiently.\n\nThese limitations are imposed by GitHub itself, not our app.</string>
